,"/farmland-atlas/florida/miami-dade-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 13 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and November to December came in under 90% of normal in 41 of 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 42% of normal in January to February and 39% in November to December. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 30% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 6197 had its driest year in 1961 at 53%.</p>"}
